  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "President Prabowo Subianto is expected to submit two names to the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) on November 25 as potential successors for the vice presidential role. The administrative process follows discussions regarding criteria such as statesmanship and alignment with the president's ideology. While Golkar has publicly proposed Sufmi Dasco Ahmad for the position, other political factions have indicated they will defer to the president's selection. The MPR has established an ad hoc committee to oversee the submission and manage potential scenarios, including the withdrawal of a nominated candidate. Although some observers initially suggested the submission date should have been earlier, officials have clarified that the official presentation is confirmed for November 25. The process involves vetting candidates to ensure they possess the necessary qualities to unify the nation while supporting the existing government's objectives and policy direction.",
